      "problem": "Simplify $10\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, but we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t10\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t(10 + 2)\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t12\\sqrt[3]{y}-7\\sqrt{y} &\n\t}\n$$",
